From the Westminster Gds.tte)
There down the quiet Channel tide
Gray ghosts of Spanish galleons glide;
Ho, ghostly Captain, priestly wrath,
Where now your high, unwaverini


faith?


Irvincible? Your courage faints,
You call on God and all the Saints;
Call louder yet, they sleep maybe;
Or were men made for liberty?
Still over there fight Freedoms sons,
The fair, faint echo Of the guns
Pulses the quiet evening air;
Uprises still the impious prayer
OF mighty battle-lusting men,
Their faith is wavering now as then;
We bow the heart. we bow the knee;
Mankind was made for liberty.


p. c. FITZGERALD.

